<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 25.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Oct 25.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 10/25/96  10/18/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    217.52    214.45    93.54	92.22     97.30</p>
<p>West	    237.93    238.69    89.84	90.13     87.00</p>
<p>Total Canada  455.45    453.14    91.57	91.10     88.70</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 10/25/96: 232.55 bcf, 10/18/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 10/25/96: 264.84 bcf, 10/18/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
